From 9d6db23b67ab16f53b3b9cff0576f5c4b6815b58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Aari Hub Build <build@aarirealty.com>
Date: Thu, 30 Jul 2026 21:37:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Producer OS shell: sidebar restructure, My Dashboard +
 Transactions restyle, honest placeholders
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Sidebar rebuilt to match aari-producer-os.html reference: Produce, Plan, Develop,
  Broker Only (server-role-gated, never CSS-hidden), Resources, Get Started.
- My Dashboard = existing Home content, relabeled and reframed with a Producer OS
  content-header. Internal id/data-panel kept as 'home' (not renamed to 'dash') after
  finding multiple hidden JS dependencies on that exact string (loading-overlay boot(),
  DOMContentLoaded hook). No query changes, GCI fix untouched.
- Transactions = existing My Deals (tx-list/viewList()), relabeled, same query.
- Database = same destination as old My CRM link (/crm.html).
- My Files, Announcements, Training Academy moved into Resources group; tx_module.html
  now wires its real loader functions (loadMyFiles/loadAnnouncements/loadTraining) onto
  these existing static items instead of injecting a duplicate sidebar group.
- 14 honest placeholders (Today, Pipeline, Calendar, Numbers, Goal Engine, Weekly Review,
  Academy Levels, Script Vault, Broker Command, Agent Inventory, Deadline Radar, Roster
  Command, Revenue and Fees, File Compliance): heading + one sentence + 'Not built yet'.
  No fake numbers, no fake controls.
- Broker Only group also carries 2 legacy items (Email, Control Panel) pointing at
  existing broker_module.html panels that had no other nav path after this rebuild.
  The other 7 legacy broker_module.html screens remain reachable via the untouched
  My Dashboard broker quick-action buttons.
- Broker Only nav items are JS-injected only after a live realty_members.role==='broker'
  check (RLS-verified 2026-07-31: agents read own row only, brokers via is_realty_broker(),
  no UPDATE on role/commission_plan/agent_split). Panel containers for those 6 screens are
  static placeholder text only (no query, no data) — queued as a hard gate before any real
  logic touches them: see AGENT-HUB-AUDIT queue.
- Fixed id collision: renamed new File Compliance placeholder from panel-compliance
  (collided with pre-existing agent-facing compliance-acknowledgments panel) to
  panel-file-compliance. Zero duplicate panel ids remain in the file, verified.
- No schema changes. No new edge function calls. No realty_transactions changes.
